Subject: [PATCH] Document the fork workflow: syncing with upstream and pull
 requests

Every team forks the class repository and sends a pull request up to
upstream main when its work is ready.

- README: set up a team fork (owner, collaborators, clone, upstream remote),
  everyday workflow inside the fork with internal pull requests and review,
  syncing with upstream (Sync fork button and git fetch/merge), conflicts,
  sending work upstream, fork troubleshooting, glossary
- README admin section: approve first-time fork workflow runs, merge commits
  only, how to review a pull request that comes from a fork, and drop the
  "branch must be up to date" requirement that would queue 12 teams
- AI_README: git model (origin/upstream, the two pull request loops, merge
  never rebase, no force push) and new common mistakes
- Pull request template: say where the pull request is going and ask for a sync

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
